---
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="nrg-footer">
  <div class="nrg-footer__inner">
    <div class="nrg-footer__notes">
      <p>Liquid Glass with No Refraction is an unofficial frosted-glass CSS kit in the iOS 27 Liquid Glass vein. It is not affiliated with Apple. Glass is blur, saturation, and inner highlights — refraction, displacement maps, and IOR are intentionally omitted.</p>
      <p>Drop in <code>nrg.css</code> (and optionally <code>nrg.js</code>). Class prefix is <code>nrg-</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="nrg-footer__bottom">
      <p>Copyright © {year}. MIT License.</p>
      <ul class="nrg-footer__legal">
        <li><a class="nrg-footer__link" href="#about">About</a></li>
        <li><a class="nrg-footer__link" href="/components">Components</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <dialog class="nrg-modal" data-nrg-modal="about">
    <div class="nrg-modal__card">
      <button type="button" class="nrg-modal__close" data-nrg-close aria-label="Close">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
      </button>
      <h3 class="nrg-modal__title">About this kit</h3>
      <div class="nrg-modal__body">
        <p>This project ships CSS tokens and frosted-glass surfaces in the iOS 27 Liquid Glass vein. Glass is <code>backdrop-filter: blur()</code> plus inner highlights — refraction is intentionally omitted.</p>
        <p>Copy <code>css/nrg.css</code> and optionally <code>css/nrg.js</code>. Prefix is <code>nrg-</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</footer>
